    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0922" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3743: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-01T00:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1,
                                1922—midnight</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 3, 2
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>72. Department’s 42, February 21, 3 p.m. Yen<anchor n="62" xml:id="d582-f1"/>
                    informed orally and in writing, stated orally today no possibility of obtaining
                    any funds during the present Cabinet crisis. He seemed very disheartened over
                    financial and political situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d582-f1" n="62" xml:id="d582-f1-content">
                <p>W. W. Yen, Chinese Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
